<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Garabet Artin Davoud Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1816–1873</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Davoud Pasha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Garabet Artin Davoud Pasha was an Ottoman official of Armenian Catholic origin who served as the first governor (mutasarrif) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-lebanon">Mount Lebanon</a> Mutasarrifate from 1861 to 1868. Appointed under the settlement agreed by the Ottoman government and the European powers after the civil war of 1860, he organised the new administration and its mixed council. He left office in 1868.</p></div>
